---
const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");

const pipeline = [
  { n: "01", stage: "Sentence", out: "\"top up our inference credits by $120\"", body: "Code, not the model, reads the amount. No amount, or two different amounts, and it stops here.", refuses: "no clear amount" },
  { n: "02", stage: "Assistant", out: "service: inference-credits", body: "The assistant may only choose a service from the spender's approved list, or say none fits.", refuses: "no matching service" },
  { n: "03", stage: "Schema", out: "{ service, amount, memo }", body: "The output must match a fixed shape. There is no address field, so an invented payee cannot be expressed.", refuses: "wrong shape" },
  { n: "04", stage: "Registry", out: "inference-credits → payee", body: "The service id must resolve in the on-chain registry and must not be suspended.", refuses: "unknown or suspended" },
  { n: "05", stage: "Policy", out: "$120 ≤ cap $250 · ≤ $560 left", body: "The contract runs the spender's policy. In policy it pays; over a limit it is held.", refuses: "over a rule" },
];

const checks = [
  ["Account paused", "the owner can freeze every payment at once"],
  ["Spender exists", "unknown keys cannot pay"],
  ["Spender paused", "one spender can be stopped without touching others"],
  ["Policy expired", "every policy has an end date"],
  ["Amount > 0", "no zero or negative transfers"],
  ["Service on allowlist", "only services approved for this spender"],
  ["Replay key unused", "the same payment cannot settle twice"],
  ["Per-payment cap", "no single payment above the cap"],
  ["Payments per period", "a ceiling on how often"],
  ["Allowance left", "a ceiling on how much per period"],
  ["Registry resolves", "unknown or suspended services revert"],
  ["Balance covers it", "the team account holds enough USDC"],
  ["Transfer", "USDC moves from the team account to the payee"],
  ["Receipt event", "written on chain for every settled payment"],
];
---

<section id="security" class="bg-surface-soft border-y border-line">
  <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-5 py-24 md:py-32 space-y-12">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <div class="eyebrow">04 · Security</div>
        <h2 class="text-[40px] sm:text-[48px] leading-[1.05] font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">
          The agent proposes. Only the contract authorizes.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-[17px] sm:text-[18px] text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-[620px]">
          You can ask the assistant to pay in plain words. What it produces is a proposal that has to survive five stages, and any one of them can refuse. The last one is the contract, and it does not trust anything before it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-3">
        {pipeline.map((p) => (
          <li class="card p-4 flex flex-col gap-3 min-w-0">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[12px] text-ink-muted">
              <span>{p.n}</span>
              <span class="text-ink">{p.stage}</span>
            </div>
            <div class={`${p.out.includes("$") ? "font-sans tabular-nums" : "font-mono"} text-[12px] text-ink bg-surface-muted rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2 break-words`}>{p.out}</div>
            <p class="text-[13px] text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed">{p.body}</p>
            <div class="mt-auto text-[12px] text-destructive">Refuses: {p.refuses}</div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <div class="space-y-5">
          <div class="eyebrow">Inside the contract</div>
          <h3 class="text-[22px] font-semibold text-ink tracking-[-0.03em] leading-snug">Every call to pay() runs the same checks, in the same order</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed">
            The app and the assistant pre-check so you see problems early, but they are a convenience. The rules that matter are in the team account contract, and a failing check means no transfer happens.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-white card p-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-ink-secondary leading-relaxed">
            <div class="eyebrow">Honest status</div>
            <p><span class="text-ink font-medium">Stellar testnet only. Not audited.</span> Use test funds.</p>
          </div>
          <a href={`${basePath}/docs/security/security-model/`} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent">Read the security model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>

        <div class="outer-technical-frame p-3 sm:p-5">
          <div class="card overflow-hidden shadow-subtle">
            <div class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-line bg-white text-ink font-mono text-[12px] font-medium break-words">pay(spender, service, amount, memo, key)</div>
            <ol class="divide-y divide-line">
              {checks.map(([k, v], i) => (
                <li class="px-4 py-2.5 flex items-baseline gap-3 text-[13px]">
                  <span class="text-ink-muted w-5 shrink-0">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
                  <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 sm:flex sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between sm:gap-4">
                    <span class="block text-ink">{k}</span>
                    <span class="block text-[12px] text-ink-muted sm:text-right">{v}</span>
                  </span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
  </div>
</section>
